  "details": "Unity 2019.4.31f1 with uptodate SDK. Publishing to windows.\nAfter Unity says the world has published successfully, I click the \"Manage World in Browser\" button in VRCSDK control panel after the successful publish - it takes me to a vrchat url (https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_4e550ebe-45af-4949-80fe-519b010a1c28), but then nothing appear on the middle panel, and no new world appears in \"My WOrlds\" either. \nWhat am I doing wrong?\nI published the same world on Android to see what would happen, it said it was a successful publish - and is now when i click the \"manage world in browser\" button it takes me to the same URL as above - https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_4e550ebe-45af-4949-80fe-519b010a1c28\nThis is pointing to an old test world i created a year ago, that i recently deleted.\nBut it has a completed different name and capacity etc to the world i was just trying to publish. \nSOmething seems very wrong. Please help!",
